# systemd-sysusers(5) declaration for the ChatGPT credential authority.
#
# Install as /usr/lib/sysusers.d/ccswitch-codex-auth.conf and apply with
#   sudo systemd-sysusers
#
# A system user with NO login shell and NO home directory of its own: the
# authority's only writable location is its StateDirectory
# (/var/lib/ccswitch-codex-auth, 0700), and every vendor subprocess it spawns has
# HOME pinned to the account's managed CODEX_HOME (see
# server/codex/auth_authority.py:_child_env). Giving this user a real home would
# create a second place a `codex` code path could drop an auth.json.
#
# The session user (tony) must NOT be a member of this group. That is the
# enforceable form of "prove the session-daemon user cannot traverse it":
#   sudo -u tony test -r /var/lib/ccswitch-codex-auth/accounts   # must fail
u ccswitch-auth - "ccswitch ChatGPT credential authority" - -
